  'gptris-digital-transport-licensing-launch-2026-10-07',
  'Gauteng launches digital system to speed up transport operating licences',
  'Business', '2026-10-07', 'Pretoria Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/10/07/gauteng-launches-digital-licensing-system-gptris-to-fast-track-public-transport-permits/',
  'Gauteng launched a digital licensing platform in Pretoria on 6 October to speed up public transport operating licences.',
  'Gauteng''s Department of Roads and Transport switched on a new digital licensing system in Pretoria on Tuesday, 6 October, aiming to cut delays in handling applications for public transport operating licences. Premier Panyaza Lesufi and Roads and Transport MEC Kedibone Diale-Tlabela attended the launch of the new tool, known by its acronym GPTRIS.

Under the new platform, operators can submit licence applications online, track their progress and pay fees digitally, instead of relying only on paper forms and in-person visits. The department says applications will follow a standard 60-day turnaround, and it is giving particular attention to e-hailing operators now that a 2025 change to transport law gave e-hailing formal recognition as a public transport service. Operators who still prefer to apply in person can continue to do so over the counter.

Diale-Tlabela said the aim is a process operators find ''faster, more transparent and responsive'', and that it should help eliminate the long queues operators have faced at licensing offices. Lesufi described the rollout as part of a broader drive to modernise government services across Gauteng.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
